{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/compare/54356a831e3d8876c69373cac884a3df2a5653f7...4637e625c99ef17c190aa471a5e51b7f646c6dfd","html_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/compare/54356a831e3d8876c69373cac884a3df2a5653f7...4637e625c99ef17c190aa471a5e51b7f646c6dfd","permalink_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/compare/OmniNode-ai:54356a8...OmniNode-ai:4637e62","diff_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/compare/54356a831e3d8876c69373cac884a3df2a5653f7...4637e625c99ef17c190aa471a5e51b7f646c6dfd.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/compare/54356a831e3d8876c69373cac884a3df2a5653f7...4637e625c99ef17c190aa471a5e51b7f646c6dfd.patch","base_commit":{"sha":"54356a831e3d8876c69373cac884a3df2a5653f7","node_id":"C_kwDOR6jjtdoAKDU0MzU2YTgzMWUzZDg4NzZjNjkzNzNjYWM4ODRhM2RmMmE1NjUzZjc","commit":{"author":{"name":"Jonah Gray","email":"jonah@omninode.ai","date":"2026-08-03T21:22:25Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-03T21:22:25Z"},"message":"fix(OMN-15651): dedicated system prompts for documentation + validator_generation; restore universal prompt invariant (#2015)\n\nVerifier finding on merged omnimarket#2012: the allowed_task_types\nexpansion 13->15 admitted `documentation` and `validator_generation`\nwithout matching `_SYSTEM_PROMPTS` entries in handler_delegation_routing.py,\nso both silently hit the generic fallback at the model-selection call\nsite (~:1567). The exemption was pinned by\ntest_prompt_subset_uses_generic_fallback_only_for_new_internal_classes\n(asserting missing == ['documentation', 'validator_generation']).\n\n- Author dedicated system prompts for both classes, grounded in how\n  task_class_contracts.v1.yaml describes them (documentation: docstring/\n  README/reference-doc authoring; validator_generation: deterministic\n  validator/contract-check authoring).\n- Restore the universal invariant: rename the test to\n  test_every_declared_task_class_has_a_dedicated_system_prompt and\n  assert missing == [] -- no allowed task class may silently fall back\n  to the generic prompt.","tree":{"sha":"75878b95a358ae17f471e55b084632c1264d2ba8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/git/trees/75878b95a358ae17f471e55b084632c1264d2ba8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/git/commits/54356a831e3d8876c69373cac884a3df2a5653f7","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqcQaRCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAtk8QAEQC8VL3/ssi8h+WjqjqhNlV\ngBMiSIx4ki9X999OzIRRhcOiGsDJnIDbyav2F0eOLjaJMdr0N0INAnTXK2Vs4U2f\nPpob4Meyoakar6RFKFuGvBf7nWEkpu/U8HCNtD8Q111k6uskdq01/FMgb2HHq2uF\nOYWY+N3kXb1+1usm1m4TSmPOnPbL2xDyN36ForRjUqorzULZcKcH4q/GHoWhEQfX\nTBTfcQPhsquzMOafIeJn3OkbvQNHshCWTJ2iVwVfvJvW1mah7bUHbYtUgdhCxbbs\nsLpFbcz0BypipZJHPbTLYlotkvxITu2cIbT3Zd5RKdfmDhC39iDnT9JrGYaW4YTY\nPbmYEZ7k3F8OYxA2fza7bCWm7Dk/W0Ko2zq9ltA7GSbuMj4+CQBF1uacBeyXJQ3Q\nyZsR0k9U+5kbC9Q5RibHWwMnGTQinvx+hBnw0Wem6wZg3HVbHnkERy9+eeaU1Rfn\nHXHD6cwGtkCOXVZa6MpLWn5YHteXqr1gmkyAgJWfVDYeIj+obrk8CtcU+QVC/8aD\nRlqfm6fIYnWZt+c/S8owcs0Ra8RAQFhpK4NjfDgRrQnCvXXCK7MNI068K0j0So3j\nF05o7HzMVtB5YTX7rR8kWDzwo6gqYErx+CMFXjyBznlPKVNhKbikph8gN0/KjeGt\nNIZp0482IfjCTt47PGCn\n=qmd2\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 75878b95a358ae17f471e55b084632c1264d2ba8\nparent 1d6d4a62c4e5f0a467d83d318252db42d2c8a590\nauthor Jonah Gray <jonah@omninode.ai> 1785792145 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785792145 -0400\n\nfix(OMN-15651): dedicated system prompts for documentation + validator_generation; restore universal prompt invariant (#2015)\n\nVerifier finding on merged omnimarket#2012: the allowed_task_types\nexpansion 13->15 admitted `documentation` and `validator_generation`\nwithout matching `_SYSTEM_PROMPTS` entries in handler_delegation_routing.py,\nso both silently hit the generic fallback at the model-selection call\nsite (~:1567). The exemption was pinned by\ntest_prompt_subset_uses_generic_fallback_only_for_new_internal_classes\n(asserting missing == ['documentation', 'validator_generation']).\n\n- Author dedicated system prompts for both classes, grounded in how\n  task_class_contracts.v1.yaml describes them (documentation: docstring/\n  README/reference-doc authoring; validator_generation: deterministic\n  validator/contract-check authoring).\n- Restore the universal invariant: rename the test to\n  test_every_declared_task_class_has_a_dedicated_system_prompt and\n  assert missing == [] -- no allowed task class may silently fall back\n  to the generic prompt.","verified_at":"2026-08-03T21:27:27Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/commits/54356a831e3d8876c69373cac884a3df2a5653f7","html_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/commit/54356a831e3d8876c69373cac884a3df2a5653f7","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/commits/54356a831e3d8876c69373cac884a3df2a5653f7/comments","author":{"login":"jonahgabriel","id":1002253,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMDIyNTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1002253?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel","html_url":"https://github.com/jonahgabriel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"1d6d4a62c4e5f0a467d83d318252db42d2c8a590","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/commits/1d6d4a62c4e5f0a467d83d318252db42d2c8a590","html_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/commit/1d6d4a62c4e5f0a467d83d318252db42d2c8a590"}]},"merge_base_commit":{"sha":"be02477811f4e21b36c7ad2ee4e573db215054a4","node_id":"C_kwDOR6jjtdoAKGJlMDI0Nzc4MTFmNGUyMWIzNmM3YWQyZWU0ZTU3M2RiMjE1MDU0YTQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Jonah Gray","email":"jonah@omninode.ai","date":"2026-07-29T15:22:40Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-29T15:22:40Z"},"message":"fix(OMN-15382): fail-closed hardening for node_dod_verify command/PR-lookup checks (#1949)\n\n* fix(OMN-15382): fail-closed hardening for node_dod_verify command/PR-lookup checks\n\nTwo independent vacuous-verdict mechanisms in node_dod_verify, both from\ntrusting untyped input without validation:\n\n1. Command-check execution (evidence_collector.py _run_command_check) ran\n   check_value verbatim via subprocess.run(cmd, shell=True) - plain sh -c,\n   no pipefail - and judged success on exit code alone. A pipe like\n   \"Recorded product receipt: ... | sha256sum\" exited 0 (vacuous GREEN,\n   hashing empty stdin) because a non-pipefail shell's pipeline exit code is\n   the LAST stage's; the same prose with no pipe exited 127 (RED, but\n   indistinguishable from a real check failure). Fixed with (a) list-form\n   execution via [\"bash\", \"-o\", \"pipefail\", \"-c\", cmd] and (b) a\n   pre-execution shape guard that rejects prose before it is ever shelled\n   out, with a distinct reason (INVALID_CHECK_VALUE_NOT_A_COMMAND).\n   Deliberately NOT a blanket \"empty stdout is RED\" rule - quiet checks like\n   grep -q still pass; a real quiet command test proves this.\n\n2. HandlerDodEvidenceGithubEffect._lookup_pr_for_ticket ran\n   `gh pr list --search <ticket_id> --state merged --json number --jq\n   .[0].number` with no --repo flag (resolving whatever repo the process\n   cwd's git remote pointed at) and blindly took the first fuzzy full-text\n   match. Root cause of a wrong PR binding (2454 instead of 2536). Fixed:\n   the lookup now requires an explicit --repo (sourced first from the\n   current dod_evidence item's id, when it follows the OCC autobind\n   dod-<owner>-<repo>-pr-<number> naming convention - zero gh calls,\n   deterministic; otherwise from REPO env / the existing repo-lookup\n   fallback), requests number+title+headRefName, and filters to candidates\n   whose title/branch contain the ticket id as an exact token. Zero or more\n   than one surviving candidate is now a fail-closed RED\n   (PR_LOOKUP_FAILED / PR_LOOKUP_AMBIGUOUS) - never a silent \"most recent\"\n   pick. LOOKUP_REPO_FOR_TICKET gets the same exact-match discipline, though\n   it still cannot discover a repo different from the invoking process cwd\n   (documented residual - this is why the id-derived binding is checked\n   first).\n\nRED-first proof: reverted these 3 source files via git stash and reran the\nnew test module against pre-fix code - all 4 shape/pipefail tests failed as\nexpected (vacuous VERIFIED where FAILED is required; RED but missing the\ndistinct reason), confirming they exercise the real bug before the fix.\n\nRipple: 4 existing tests in test_handler_dod_evidence_github_effect.py\nencoded the old ambiguous-search wire contract (bare jq-extracted string\nstdout, no --repo) and are updated to the new JSON-array + --repo contract;\n7 new tests added there for the ambiguous/mismatched/missing-repo/\nid-derived-binding cases.\n\nOMN-15382\n\n* docs(OMN-15382): avoid a bare ticket-shaped substring in a docstring example\n\n* chore(OMN-15382): retrigger occ-preflight now that contracts/OMN-15382.yaml is bound in OCC\n\n* fix(OMN-15382): cwd-aware shape guard + case-insensitive/repo-cardinality lookup fixes\n\nVerifier-rejected lane B2 remediation:\n\n1. Move the command-check shape guard (_invalid_check_value_reason) to run\n   AFTER cwd resolution and make it cwd-aware. Previously it ran before\n   run_cwd was computed and judged a relative first token (e.g.\n   \"./verify.sh\") via a bare shutil.which(), which only ever inspects this\n   process actual cwd/PATH -- never the checks declared cwd:. That produced\n   false-RED (INVALID_CHECK_VALUE_NOT_A_COMMAND) on a legitimate,\n   pre-existing supported shape (OMN-10078 relative-script + cwd:).\n\n2. _lookup_pr_for_ticket / _exact_ticket_token_candidates: match the ticket\n   token case-insensitively so the headRefName arm actually fires against\n   conventionally-lowercased branch names, not just uppercase PR titles.\n\n3. _lookup_repo_for_ticket: judge ambiguity on the distinct repo set, not\n   the raw PR-candidate count, so two merged PRs for one ticket in the SAME\n   repo no longer false-fails REPO_LOOKUP_AMBIGUOUS.\n\nAddresses CodeRabbit PR #1949 comments 3675341071 (Major), 3675341023,\n3675341061 (Minor) -- all three unresolved threads blocking gate /\nCodeRabbit Thread Check.\n\nNew regression tests cover all three fixes; full node_dod_verify suite\n(216 tests) green on .200.","tree":{"sha":"8bede4e520a6acbe8e0a0342c1fbe2b79410af04","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/git/trees/8bede4e520a6acbe8e0a0342c1fbe2b79410af04"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/git/commits/be02477811f4e21b36c7ad2ee4e573db215054a4","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqahrACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAkwkQAHfPF9BT3DsWkDKzNTh5DSMd\nwYTqxg88lfiRXrm9+puadB+ubZXhdx/o5C/ln5VU1GC+GXSjIK/4j0Ta+Mi6wn8T\nlqVjTjuqdwWkV7XdSumblMSdCjB1yeQy13LPOvljgDQwfRF7PWwfIeYOmSNHLKTy\nvxi/+v0mcdjAMTPKO+x8mr1KbeX/0/TPQHVIHiMRmHJzTO9C+ZqFAVdcD6Uy+Liz\nfjUB7KQl/nNk93fRqleT/2bK/RY/ZueJdqdim3lRYC3+ib+AWia6nXYQlHsITiRN\ns6cLLbTD1s7Xh0ebVdWeGjJJ78sLDJeaqDuL+oqOF5gcJ2Jsh+xFYr40/DIP5t1V\nksAzcYZmK0H1nBV1zSS6fs7wikaA4g8uxLEYt2z2UPUkCQv/L1GQtaH1LF/X5BvL\n35iIUJvK9H+5BgTUriRncTOSU9MPfJ3ZA3/bn7vna+WoCzFF5ZJLW+vMfUN2JYhs\n+CCpV1jS2Ou6DxjsDHuPm/ftwP81DjsQrdFMgmnWxnUoqAkQHTvR0QoWDRLrY6Tj\nKapWnoaDVLSA5IhZI88sdCy+ygomvNeUUGIFUiiqz2W4ZSxgIGSQtqH+jK9B1wmU\nvE0mhrLoYFDLDj4w5atT8wXHWHIW/xQTCrVAgxWQQ6VvPE1wJM4LY/FmVE6fQyMO\nJClZe7Sk97QcKWqD3SWj\n=YB4A\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 8bede4e520a6acbe8e0a0342c1fbe2b79410af04\nparent 944c9f2fd492bc306f858f264b4ab4e47f73f9b0\nauthor Jonah Gray <jonah@omninode.ai> 1785338560 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785338560 -0400\n\nfix(OMN-15382): fail-closed hardening for node_dod_verify command/PR-lookup checks (#1949)\n\n* fix(OMN-15382): fail-closed hardening for node_dod_verify command/PR-lookup checks\n\nTwo independent vacuous-verdict mechanisms in node_dod_verify, both from\ntrusting untyped input without validation:\n\n1. Command-check execution (evidence_collector.py _run_command_check) ran\n   check_value verbatim via subprocess.run(cmd, shell=True) - plain sh -c,\n   no pipefail - and judged success on exit code alone. A pipe like\n   \"Recorded product receipt: ... | sha256sum\" exited 0 (vacuous GREEN,\n   hashing empty stdin) because a non-pipefail shell's pipeline exit code is\n   the LAST stage's; the same prose with no pipe exited 127 (RED, but\n   indistinguishable from a real check failure). Fixed with (a) list-form\n   execution via [\"bash\", \"-o\", \"pipefail\", \"-c\", cmd] and (b) a\n   pre-execution shape guard that rejects prose before it is ever shelled\n   out, with a distinct reason (INVALID_CHECK_VALUE_NOT_A_COMMAND).\n   Deliberately NOT a blanket \"empty stdout is RED\" rule - quiet checks like\n   grep -q still pass; a real quiet command test proves this.\n\n2. HandlerDodEvidenceGithubEffect._lookup_pr_for_ticket ran\n   `gh pr list --search <ticket_id> --state merged --json number --jq\n   .[0].number` with no --repo flag (resolving whatever repo the process\n   cwd's git remote pointed at) and blindly took the first fuzzy full-text\n   match. Root cause of a wrong PR binding (2454 instead of 2536). Fixed:\n   the lookup now requires an explicit --repo (sourced first from the\n   current dod_evidence item's id, when it follows the OCC autobind\n   dod-<owner>-<repo>-pr-<number> naming convention - zero gh calls,\n   deterministic; otherwise from REPO env / the existing repo-lookup\n   fallback), requests number+title+headRefName, and filters to candidates\n   whose title/branch contain the ticket id as an exact token. Zero or more\n   than one surviving candidate is now a fail-closed RED\n   (PR_LOOKUP_FAILED / PR_LOOKUP_AMBIGUOUS) - never a silent \"most recent\"\n   pick. LOOKUP_REPO_FOR_TICKET gets the same exact-match discipline, though\n   it still cannot discover a repo different from the invoking process cwd\n   (documented residual - this is why the id-derived binding is checked\n   first).\n\nRED-first proof: reverted these 3 source files via git stash and reran the\nnew test module against pre-fix code - all 4 shape/pipefail tests failed as\nexpected (vacuous VERIFIED where FAILED is required; RED but missing the\ndistinct reason), confirming they exercise the real bug before the fix.\n\nRipple: 4 existing tests in test_handler_dod_evidence_github_effect.py\nencoded the old ambiguous-search wire contract (bare jq-extracted string\nstdout, no --repo) and are updated to the new JSON-array + --repo contract;\n7 new tests added there for the ambiguous/mismatched/missing-repo/\nid-derived-binding cases.\n\nOMN-15382\n\n* docs(OMN-15382): avoid a bare ticket-shaped substring in a docstring example\n\n* chore(OMN-15382): retrigger occ-preflight now that contracts/OMN-15382.yaml is bound in OCC\n\n* fix(OMN-15382): cwd-aware shape guard + case-insensitive/repo-cardinality lookup fixes\n\nVerifier-rejected lane B2 remediation:\n\n1. Move the command-check shape guard (_invalid_check_value_reason) to run\n   AFTER cwd resolution and make it cwd-aware. Previously it ran before\n   run_cwd was computed and judged a relative first token (e.g.\n   \"./verify.sh\") via a bare shutil.which(), which only ever inspects this\n   process actual cwd/PATH -- never the checks declared cwd:. That produced\n   false-RED (INVALID_CHECK_VALUE_NOT_A_COMMAND) on a legitimate,\n   pre-existing supported shape (OMN-10078 relative-script + cwd:).\n\n2. _lookup_pr_for_ticket / _exact_ticket_token_candidates: match the ticket\n   token case-insensitively so the headRefName arm actually fires against\n   conventionally-lowercased branch names, not just uppercase PR titles.\n\n3. _lookup_repo_for_ticket: judge ambiguity on the distinct repo set, not\n   the raw PR-candidate count, so two merged PRs for one ticket in the SAME\n   repo no longer false-fails REPO_LOOKUP_AMBIGUOUS.\n\nAddresses CodeRabbit PR #1949 comments 3675341071 (Major), 3675341023,\n3675341061 (Minor) -- all three unresolved threads blocking gate /\nCodeRabbit Thread Check.\n\nNew regression tests cover all three fixes; full node_dod_verify suite\n(216 tests) green on .200.","verified_at":"2026-07-29T15:22:41Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/commits/be02477811f4e21b36c7ad2ee4e573db215054a4","html_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/commit/be02477811f4e21b36c7ad2ee4e573db215054a4","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/commits/be02477811f4e21b36c7ad2ee4e573db215054a4/comments","author":{"login":"jonahgabriel","id":1002253,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMDIyNTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1002253?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel","html_url":"https://github.com/jonahgabriel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.c